From: OpenHarmony Compile Agent
Subject: [PATCH] Fix compile flags for OHOS with musl

This patch documents the required compile and linker flags for building
Perl XS modules on OpenHarmony with musl libc.

Problem:
1. Perl's default CCFLAGS doesn't include musl header path
2. Linker can't find CRT files (crti.o, crtbeginS.o, etc.)

Solution:
1. Add -I/path/to/musl/include to CCFLAGS
2. Use -nostartfiles -nodefaultlibs to skip CRT

Note: This patch is for documentation. Actual Makefiles were
modified manually using sed commands during the build process.

---

--- a/Makefile.PL
+++ b/Makefile.PL
@@ -0,0 +0,0 @@
+# Add OHOS-specific compile flags
+my $musl_inc = '/storage/Users/currentUser/usr/local/include';
+my $musl_lib = '/storage/Users/currentUser/usr/local/lib';
+
+# Add musl include path to CCFLAGS
+$CCFLAGS .= " -I$musl_inc";
+
+# Use nostartfiles/nodefaultlibs for musl linking
+$LDDLFLAGS .= " -nostartfiles -nodefaultlibs -L$musl_lib";

The same modifications were applied to all sub-module Makefiles
(Byte, CN, EBCDIC, JP, KR, Symbol, TW, Unicode).

